Negative control for ONE bar in two states (`G9 unified` · `AC2.2`).

Gives the armed state a root of its own carrying the bar's own handle, and
leaves everything else — the same menu, the same transport, the same rail row,
the same scene — so the only claim that can go red is the ruled one: the bar is
ONE node that morphs, never a second bar mounted beside the first when a track
arms.

Re-targeted 2026-08-13 after the `R7-10`/`R7-8` restructure: the split-component
form this control used to take patched `ScenarioMediaBar` into a `ScenarioBar`
that no longer exists in that shape. Same claim, same red, current source.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the one-bar case — exactly one node answers to the bar's own handle,
armed or live, and it is the same node before and after.

